@title Place macro: a click on the macro's name picks it (1920x1080)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
# Acceptance A-01: rows swallowed clicks on their own text (selectable labels), so the
# macro list could only be picked by clicking the thin padding at the row's edge.
click_text "New project"
wait 20
key ctrl+k
# The command, not a macro's name (a name picks that macro already): the list stays unpicked.
text "place macro"
wait 5
key Enter
wait 10
expect "No macro picked"
# The list is longer than the window: search, then click the row's own text.
# The Place macro window docks at the right edge: its search field is at x 1205 at 1366 wide and x 1759 at 1920 wide (a click outside the window would take the keyboard away, so each size has its own file).
click 1759 103
wait 4
text motor starter dol
wait 5
click_text "Motor starter DOL" Label
wait 10
expect_not "No macro picked"
expect "Keep the macro's wire numbers"
shot macro-picked
click_text Place Button
wait 20
expect_scene "-K1"
shot macro-placed
